# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Reverse-engineering material — NEVER PUBLISH
#
# The official application's APK and everything derived from it (decompiled
# code, smali, resources) stay strictly local. This repository only holds code
# written independently from the observed specification.
#
# This rule is about the *manufacturer's* APK. The release workflow builds our
# own APK on the runner and uploads it straight to the GitHub release, so it
# never passes through git.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.apk
jadx-out/
smali-out/
dexdir/
*.dex
*.jar
*.btsnoop
hci.btsnoop

# Exception: the Gradle wrapper is a legitimate project binary, without which
# ./gradlew does not work on a fresh clone.
!android/gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar

# Build artefacts. `go build ./...` inside probe/ drops the binary next to
# the source, so the name has to match exactly or an ordinary build dirties
# the working tree.
build/bin/
probe/peatsprobe
probe/peatsprobe.exe

# The built frontend is ignored, but the directory itself must exist on a
# fresh clone: main.go does //go:embed all:frontend/dist, and Wails loads that
# package to generate its bindings *before* the frontend is compiled. With no
# directory the embed pattern matches nothing and the build fails before it
# starts. The `all:` prefix is what makes a lone dotfile enough to satisfy it.
peatsaudio/frontend/dist/*
!peatsaudio/frontend/dist/.gitkeep

peatsaudio/frontend/node_modules/
peatsaudio/frontend/wailsjs/
node_modules/

# Release staging, produced by .github/workflows/release.yml.
# Anchored: an unanchored "dist/" would also swallow peatsaudio/frontend/dist,
# whose tracked .gitkeep the Wails build depends on.
/dist/

# Misc
*.log
.DS_Store

# Android
android/.gradle/
android/build/
android/app/build/
android/local.properties
android/.idea/
android/.kotlin/
*.iml

# Signing keys, wherever they land: a release keystore in git would let anyone
# sign an update that installs over ours.
*.jks
*.keystore

# peatsctl, built where CLAUDE.md says to build it (cd peatsaudio) or at the
# root.
/peatsctl
/peatsctl.exe
peatsaudio/peatsctl
peatsaudio/peatsctl.exe

# Worktrees Claude Code creates for parallel agents.
.claude/worktrees/
